    <summary>OpenBao - manage, store, and distribute secrets such as tokens, passwords, certificates, and encryption keys.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
[OpenBao](https://openbao.org/) is an open source, community-driven fork of HashiCorp Vault, managed by the Linux Foundation. It exists to provide a software solution to manage, store, and distribute sensitive data including secrets, certificates, and keys.

This package downloads the official OpenBao release archive from the
[OpenBao GitHub releases](https://github.com/openbao/openbao/releases) and verifies its SHA256 checksum before installing.

## What you get

The package installs the OpenBao command-line interface. After installation the
`bao` command is available on your `PATH` (Chocolatey creates a shim automatically):

```powershell
bao version
bao server -dev
```

## Notes

* 64-bit only. OpenBao does not publish a 32-bit (x86) Windows build. Both
  `x86_64` (amd64) and `arm64` Windows builds are supported and selected
  automatically based on your processor architecture.
* This is an unofficial, community-maintained Chocolatey package. Package
  problems should be reported on the
  [package source repository](https://github.com/jaxzin/choco-openbao/issues);
  problems with OpenBao itself belong on the
  [OpenBao issue tracker](https://github.com/openbao/openbao/issues).
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/openbao/openbao/releases/tag/v2.5.4</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
